    "title": "The Cat in Boots",
    "level": "Level 2",
    "text": "SC01_ST01_N = A miller had three sons.\nSC01_ST02_N = When he died, the oldest got the mill, the second got a donkey, and the youngest got only a cat.\nSC01_ST03_N = The youngest son felt very sad.\nSC01_ST04_N = \"What can I do with just a cat?\" he said.\nSC02_ST01_N = Then the Cat said, \"Do not worry.\nSC02_ST02_N = Give me a bag and a pair of boots.\nSC02_ST03_N = I will help you.\"\nSC02_ST04_N = The son was not sure, but he had seen the Cat do many clever tricks before.\nSC02_ST05_N = He began to feel hopeful and agreed.\nSC03_ST01_N = The Cat put on his boots and went to the woods.\nSC03_ST02_N = He put some food in his bag and lay down as if he were dead.\nSC04_ST01_N = Soon, a young rabbit came to look inside the bag.\nSC04_ST02_N = The Cat quickly pulled the string, caught it, and went to the King's palace.\nSC05_ST01_N = The Cat bowed and said, \"This is a gift from Lord Carabas.\"\nSC05_ST02_N = The King was very pleased with the gift.\nSC06_ST01_N = Another day, the Cat caught two birds in the same way.\nSC06_ST02_N = He brought them to the King and said, \"These are from Lord Carabas.\"\nSC07_ST01_N = For many days, the Cat brought more animals to the King.\nSC07_ST02_N = The King began to like the Lord Carabas and gave the Cat some gold.\nSC08_ST01_N = One day, the King went for a ride by the river.\nSC08_ST02_N = The Cat said, \"Master, today your fortune will change.\nSC08_ST03_N = Come with me to the river.\"\nSC08_ST04_N = The young man followed him.\nSC09_ST01_N = \"Go into the water,\" said the Cat.\nSC09_ST02_N = While his master was bathing, the Cat hid his clothes under a stone.\nSC10_ST01_N = Soon the King's coach came by.\nSC10_ST02_N = The Cat cried, \"Help!\nSC10_ST03_N = The Lord Carabas is drowning!\nSC10_ST04_N = Thieves stole his clothes!\"\nSC11_ST01_N = The King's guards pulled the young man from the water.\nSC11_ST02_N = The King gave him fine clothes.\nSC11_ST03_N = He looked very handsome, and the Princess liked him at once.\nSC11_ST04_N = The King asked him to join them in the coach.\nSC12_ST01_N = Meanwhile, the Cat ran ahead and met some workers cutting grass.\nSC12_ST02_N = \"If the King asks,\" he said, \"tell him this land belongs to the Lord Carabas.\"\nSC13_ST01_N = The King passed and asked, \"Whose land is this?\"\nSC13_ST02_N = \"The Lord Carabas's!\" the worker answered.\nSC13_ST03_N = The King was impressed.\nSC13_ST04_N = He believed that the Lord was a very wealthy man.\nSC14_ST01_N = The Cat went on and told more workers the same thing.\nSC14_ST02_N = He did this in fields of grain and across the wide countryside.\nSC14_ST03_N = So everywhere the King looked, people said the land belonged to the Lord.\nSC15_ST01_N = At last, the Cat came to a grand castle.\nSC15_ST02_N = A rich Giant lived there, and all the lands the Cat had just passed by belonged to him.\nSC16_ST01_N = The Giant had the power to change his shape.\nSC16_ST02_N = The Cat said, \"I heard you can turn into any animal.\"\nSC16_ST03_N = \"That is true,\"answered the Giant.\nSC16_ST04_N = At once, he became a huge lion.\nSC16_ST05_N = The Cat quickly jumped back in fear.\nSC17_ST01_N = Then the Cat said, \"That is amazing!\nSC17_ST02_N = But can you turn into something very small, like a mouse?\"\nSC17_ST03_N = The Giant laughed and turned into a tiny mouse to show off.\nSC18_ST01_N = The Cat jumped on the mouse.\nSC18_ST02_N = Now the grand castle belonged to his lord.\nSC19_ST01_N = The King arrived and was impressed by the castle.\nSC19_ST02_N = \"You are very rich, Lord Carabas,\" he said.\nSC20_ST01_N = Lord Carabas married the Princess that very day.\nSC20_ST02_N = The Cat became a great lord and lived happily ever after.",
    "scenes": [
      {
        "sceneId": "SC01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC01_ST01_N",
            "text": "A miller had three sons."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC01_ST02_N",
            "text": "When he died, the oldest got the mill, the second got a donkey, and the youngest got only a cat."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC01_ST03_N",
            "text": "The youngest son felt very sad."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC01_ST04_N",
            "text": "\"What can I do with just a cat?\" he said."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC02",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC02_ST01_N",
            "text": "Then the Cat said, \"Do not worry."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC02_ST02_N",
            "text": "Give me a bag and a pair of boots."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC02_ST03_N",
            "text": "I will help you.\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC02_ST04_N",
            "text": "The son was not sure, but he had seen the Cat do many clever tricks before."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC02_ST05_N",
            "text": "He began to feel hopeful and agreed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC03",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC03_ST01_N",
            "text": "The Cat put on his boots and went to the woods."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC03_ST02_N",
            "text": "He put some food in his bag and lay down as if he were dead."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC04",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC04_ST01_N",
            "text": "Soon, a young rabbit came to look inside the bag."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC04_ST02_N",
            "text": "The Cat quickly pulled the string, caught it, and went to the King's palace."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC05",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC05_ST01_N",
            "text": "The Cat bowed and said, \"This is a gift from Lord Carabas.\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC05_ST02_N",
            "text": "The King was very pleased with the gift."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC06",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC06_ST01_N",
            "text": "Another day, the Cat caught two birds in the same way."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC06_ST02_N",
            "text": "He brought them to the King and said, \"These are from Lord Carabas.\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC07",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC07_ST01_N",
            "text": "For many days, the Cat brought more animals to the King."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC07_ST02_N",
            "text": "The King began to like the Lord Carabas and gave the Cat some gold."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC08",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC08_ST01_N",
            "text": "One day, the King went for a ride by the river."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC08_ST02_N",
            "text": "The Cat said, \"Master, today your fortune will change."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC08_ST03_N",
            "text": "Come with me to the river.\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC08_ST04_N",
            "text": "The young man followed him."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC09",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC09_ST01_N",
            "text": "\"Go into the water,\" said the Cat."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC09_ST02_N",
            "text": "While his master was bathing, the Cat hid his clothes under a stone."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC10",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC10_ST01_N",
            "text": "Soon the King's coach came by."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC10_ST02_N",
            "text": "The Cat cried, \"Help!"
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC10_ST03_N",
            "text": "The Lord Carabas is drowning!"
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC10_ST04_N",
            "text": "Thieves stole his clothes!\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC11",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC11_ST01_N",
            "text": "The King's guards pulled the young man from the water."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC11_ST02_N",
            "text": "The King gave him fine clothes."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC11_ST03_N",
            "text": "He looked very handsome, and the Princess liked him at once."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC11_ST04_N",
            "text": "The King asked him to join them in the coach."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC12",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC12_ST01_N",
            "text": "Meanwhile, the Cat ran ahead and met some workers cutting grass."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC12_ST02_N",
            "text": "\"If the King asks,\" he said, \"tell him this land belongs to the Lord Carabas.\""
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC13",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC13_ST01_N",
            "text": "The King passed and asked, \"Whose land is this?\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC13_ST02_N",
            "text": "\"The Lord Carabas's!\" the worker answered."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC13_ST03_N",
            "text": "The King was impressed."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC13_ST04_N",
            "text": "He believed that the Lord was a very wealthy man."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC14",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC14_ST01_N",
            "text": "The Cat went on and told more workers the same thing."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC14_ST02_N",
            "text": "He did this in fields of grain and across the wide countryside."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC14_ST03_N",
            "text": "So everywhere the King looked, people said the land belonged to the Lord."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC15",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC15_ST01_N",
            "text": "At last, the Cat came to a grand castle."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC15_ST02_N",
            "text": "A rich Giant lived there, and all the lands the Cat had just passed by belonged to him."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC16",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC16_ST01_N",
            "text": "The Giant had the power to change his shape."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC16_ST02_N",
            "text": "The Cat said, \"I heard you can turn into any animal.\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC16_ST03_N",
            "text": "\"That is true,\"answered the Giant."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC16_ST04_N",
            "text": "At once, he became a huge lion."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC16_ST05_N",
            "text": "The Cat quickly jumped back in fear."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC17",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC17_ST01_N",
            "text": "Then the Cat said, \"That is amazing!"
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC17_ST02_N",
            "text": "But can you turn into something very small, like a mouse?\""
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC17_ST03_N",
            "text": "The Giant laughed and turned into a tiny mouse to show off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC18",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC18_ST01_N",
            "text": "The Cat jumped on the mouse."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC18_ST02_N",
            "text": "Now the grand castle belonged to his lord."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC19",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC19_ST01_N",
            "text": "The King arrived and was impressed by the castle."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC19_ST02_N",
            "text": "\"You are very rich, Lord Carabas,\" he said."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "sceneId": "SC20",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC20_ST01_N",
            "text": "Lord Carabas married the Princess that very day."
          },
          {
            "sentenceId": "SC20_ST02_N",
            "text": "The Cat became a great lord and lived happily ever after."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
